<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="53251" href="schedule/2014/fall/DANC/310/53251.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2014" href="schedule/2014.xml">2014</calendarYear><term id="120148" href="schedule/2014/fall.xml">Fall 2014</term><subject id="DANC" href="schedule/2014/fall/DANC.xml">Dance</subject><course id="310" href="schedule/2014/fall/DANC/310.xml">World Dance Forms</course></parents><sectionNumber>HH1</sectionNumber><sectionTitle>Hip Hop</sectionTitle><creditHours>1 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>Advanced Level Hip Hop Class. Hip-Hop dance technique will consist of the study and practice of Urban dance forms grounded in hip-hop culture.  Students will explore the multiple dimensions of hip-hop dance as they train in the fundamentals of each form, learn its respective historical context, and access ways of incorporating individual ideas and lived experiences into their dancing.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Not intended for Dance or Dance major(s).</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>Open (Restricted)</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2014-08-25Z</startDate><endDate>2014-12-10Z</endDate><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LAB">Laboratory</type><start>09:00 AM</start><end>10:20 AM</end><daysOfTheWeek>TR     </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>2500</roomNumber><buildingName>Krannert Center for Perf Arts</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Zbikowski" firstName="A">Zbikowski, A</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>